findings=[
 {'id':'Q334','title':'Welding advertises typed page zoom that the public Weld adapter refuses','source':'crates/inker/engines/weld-engine/src/welding_0_15.rs:987;crates/inker/engines/weld-engine/src/producer.rs:279;crates/inker/inker/src/surface_engine.rs:1067','status':'verified current capability projection and inherited trait default; full Welding/CEF feature not executed','evidence':'Welding 0.15 map_capabilities unconditionally sets document.page_zoom to Supported. WeldSurface and WeldProducer expose no set_page_zoom forwarding, so the public WebSurface inherits Inker\'s explicit Unsupported return. WeldingSurface::apply_settings can set legacy zoom, but the typed trait contract explicitly distinguishes that from set_page_zoom and its state/bounds result. This is a false capability claim rather than an Ok result on a refused operation. Scrying\'s neighboring capability projection already makes this distinction.','diagnostics':[trace_name],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Either wire typed zoom and its bounds/result through WeldSurface/WeldProducer/Welding, or narrow the capability until that path exists. This is bounded and should not become an unrelated CEF feature expansion.'}},
 {'id':'Q335','title':'The public BM25 zero-limit query panics whenever it finds a match','source':'crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/bm25.rs:140,189,190','status':'reproduced through fresh public Bm25Index over exact retained suppliers','evidence':'search allocates/ranks hits and, when hits.len()>limit, partitions at limit-1. A matching query with limit=0 underflows/panics, while the missing-term zero-limit control returns empty and a limit-one positive control succeeds. Both higher-level DocumentIndex and TrailIndex clamp their own limits to one, so they hide the core API bug rather than reproducing this crash in their normal route. No current direct product caller passing zero was established.','diagnostics':['search_boundaries_probe_v3_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Return an empty core result for zero or validate the limit at this public API. Preserve higher-level policy separately.'}},
 {'id':'Q336','title':'A custom-stemmed trail projection reopens as current with different search results','source':'crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/index.rs:168,186,299;crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/spec.rs:114;crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/tokenize.rs:23','status':'reproduced using fresh TrailIndex persistent rebuild and open on disposable fixtures','evidence':'IndexConfig permits a stemming function and persistence together. write always stamps SearchIndexSpec::current, which names the default tokenizer; Projection stores scoring config and raw documents but no custom tokenizer identity. open accepts that sidecar and rebuilds postings with Tokenizer::new. A document titled running under a trim-ing stemmer answers runn before close, but open succeeds and returns no runn hit afterward (running still matches). This contradicts both the source promise that stemmed indices are reminted instead of reopened and the one-build-path claim that reopening cannot rank differently. The Genet segmentation profile is also exported but absent from the sidecar; no cross-version profile test was run.','diagnostics':['search_boundaries_probe_v3_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Refuse persistent custom hooks without a stable profile, or retain an explicit named tokenizer profile and require its resolver on open. Do not silently invent a serialization identity for an arbitrary function pointer.'}},
 {'id':'Q337','title':'Persistent trail rebuilding recursively removes all contents of an unverified caller path','source':'crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/index.rs:286,288;crates/intel/eidetic-search/examples/eidetic-recall.rs:291','status':'reproduced only with marker-identified disposable fixtures under the approved target; no user data or live store touched','evidence':'TrailIndex::write calls remove_dir_all on the complete supplied path before recreating two cache files. It checks neither owned cache markers nor whether unrelated files exist. A disposable unrelated marker disappears after a successful public rebuild; the transient rebuild control preserves the same kind of marker. The private method does describe replacing whatever was there, so the behavior is not undocumented there, but the public cache API and example --index override provide no path-ownership boundary. Pointing the override at another directory can delete its removable contents; no live Fjall deletion or actual source-tree overwrite was executed. Errors after removal can also leave the old cache unavailable, which is source evidence rather than a fault-injection receipt.','diagnostics':['search_boundaries_probe_v3_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Confine replacement to the cache files this implementation owns and stage/replace them, or require an owned directory marker before whole-directory removal. Keep any larger cache transaction redesign documented if it would prolong the audit.'}},
 {'id':'Q338','title':'BM25 silently wraps the 257th field into field zero','source':'crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/bm25.rs:56,92,121','status':'reproduced through fresh public Bm25Index; normal three-field adapters are outside the failing shape','evidence':'new accepts any weights.len(), while add_document casts every enumerated field index to u8 without admission checks. With 257 fields, the sole alpha token in field index256 is stored/scored under field0, so weight256=1 and all other weights=0 yields no hit. The equivalent single-field control yields one. Length/accounting are indexed through the same truncated field, not only the posting tag. This contradicts the generic weights.len()-fields surface; no in-tree consumer with more than three fields was established.','diagnostics':['search_boundaries_probe_v3_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Use a wide field index internally or refuse unsupported field counts explicitly before adding documents. Do not present silently truncated storage as an arbitrary-field scorer.'}},
]
for f in findings:f['verification']=NAME
