rows=[
 ('Weld host and version adapter have distinct ownership','The default crate is an Inker host seam; the opt-in Welding 0.15 feature wraps a concrete producer.', ['crates/inker/engines/weld-engine/Cargo.toml','crates/inker/engines/weld-engine/src/lib.rs','crates/inker/engines/weld-engine/src/engine.rs'], 'Runtime/profile/subprocess startup/import-cache policy remains host-owned. Module prose still says the CEF distribution never resolves into Mere and describes an is_new bit, despite the opt-in dependency and resource_epoch/owned-payload implementation. Default-only claims should be bounded explicitly.'),
 ('Weld and Graft duplicate most erased host forwarding','Two Surface traits and Producer impls repeat navigation/input/frame/default refusal plumbing.', ['crates/inker/engines/weld-engine/src/producer.rs','crates/inker/engines/graft-engine/src/producer.rs'], 'Independent host seams are justified by distinct composites, but nearly identical forwarding/default recipes can drift: Weld has required capability projection and typed find/cookie/auth/permission methods; Graft has optional native accessibility. A common helper would need to preserve those actual differences rather than erase them into one hopeful interface.'),
 ('Owned Welding native frame transport preserves allocation custody','Type erasure carries NativeFrame intact and wrong-type recovery returns the complete SurfaceFrame.', ['crates/inker/engines/weld-engine/src/welding_0_15.rs'], 'The direct adapter emits None for generic sync metadata but the backend-owned payload still retains its native descriptor. Do not infer unsynchronized import without reading the selected importer. resource_epoch comes from allocation generation and is separate from content generation.'),
 ('Welding instance capability translation narrows several upstream claims','Construction config controls permissions/auth/download admission; unsupported capture/CDP/PDF/IME/accessibility remain explicit.', ['crates/inker/engines/weld-engine/src/welding_0_15.rs'], 'Q334 finds typed zoom overclaimed despite those careful branches. cookie change_events copies caps.cookie_change_events, while no CookieStoreChanged projection exists in map_event/map_navigation_event; future/other events become diagnostics. Concrete upstream support/event production must be checked before promoting that second mismatch.'),
 ('Weld richer input preserves information that legacy paths omit','Mouse PointerEvent carries changed/held buttons/modifiers; raw keyboard is followed by supplied text as CHAR events.', ['crates/inker/engines/weld-engine/src/welding_0_15.rs'], 'Source tests cover right button dispatch, modifier retention, two contacts, typed unsupported extra buttons and failure at the first rejected key event. These tests were read, not run with CEF suppliers. Legacy MouseEvent has default modifiers and separate wheel translation; these are actual distinct contracts rather than proof that every input path has equal fidelity.'),
 ('Welding find correlation is held as one latest query','WeldingSurface stores active_find_query and maps a FindResult using whatever value is current when polled.', ['crates/inker/engines/weld-engine/src/welding_0_15.rs'], 'The public callback shape carries count/ordinal/final_update without a query ID. A queued old result can be labeled with a later query unless the producer guarantees retirement. The source test maps one static query only. Document the producer correlation requirement before redesigning the protocol.'),
 ('Trail and document recall share one BM25 engine but repeat adapter recipes','Transient grouped SearchDocument and persisted per-visit TrailDoc use Bm25Index and the same Tokenizer.', ['crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/document.rs','crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/index.rs','crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/bm25.rs'], 'Grouping/alias lookup versus visit columns are real different projections. Field indices/counts, exact absolute-address predicate, IDF exact lane and hit mapping are independently repeated. The two scheme-detection helpers are currently textually equivalent; there is no need to call both one authority to acknowledge shared scoring.'),
 ('Core scorer bounds differ from its safer adapters','Bm25Index publicly accepts arbitrary fields and limit while wrappers clamp limits and supply three fields.', ['crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/bm25.rs','crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/index.rs','crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/document.rs'], 'Q335/Q338 exercise public core behavior hidden by wrapper constraints. The scorer has no config validation for finite/meaningful k1/b/weights; that is a follow-up contract choice, not a benchmarked product failure. Four original scorer unit tests pass freshly.'),
 ('Tokenizer sharing stops short of persisted profile identity','One tokenizer composes Genet word boundaries with connector splitting/lowercase/optional hook.', ['crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/tokenize.rs','crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/spec.rs','crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/index.rs'], 'Candidate and scoring lanes actually share this implementation. Q336 shows persistence stamps a default name for custom stemming, and SEGMENTATION_PROFILE is not included in the compatibility object. Dictionaries remain openly deferred; no claim of language-specific segmentation is made.'),
 ('Cache replacement exceeds the owned file boundary','TrailIndex persistence considers the whole supplied directory disposable.', ['crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/index.rs','crates/intel/eidetic-search/examples/eidetic-recall.rs'], 'Q337 executes removal of a test marker only. Index/spec writes are separate and non-atomic, and all read-side filesystem errors map to Missing in open/read_sidecar; permissions and missing are therefore conflated. The example remints on Missing, increasing the importance of constrained cache ownership.'),
 ('Search index sidecar is format compatibility rather than source freshness','Spec names engine/field version/tokenizer, with a separate typed codicil path.', ['crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/spec.rs','crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/index.rs'], 'It does not bind projection bytes to a particular trace revision/store/owner. This is honestly derived local state, but callers must rebuild after corpus changes; accepted current spec alone is not evidence of current corpus completeness. Sidecar describe omits tokenizer despite comparing it, reducing mismatch diagnostic detail.'),
 ('Candidate index defines prefix membership separately from rank','Flat sorted token arrays and postings answer AND across token prefixes.', ['crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/candidates.rs'], 'This is deliberately not the BM25 disjunction or a substring scan. Key identity is caller-owned: duplicate input keys can still emerge through separate record IDs, despite keys-without-repeats prose. memory_bytes counts occupied arrays/blob and explicitly excludes keys; vector capacity/header overhead is not counted. The ignored 42k timing test is not a current performance receipt.'),
 ('Fusion has one implementation for two and many lanes','fuse delegates to fuse_many over ranked URL lists.', ['crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/fusion.rs'], 'This is real shared policy. Five original tests pass freshly. The generic lane accepts duplicate URLs, accumulates their score repeatedly and records the last rank, so callers must deduplicate; the example explicitly does. Zero weight retains lane-only zero-score URLs, as its source test documents. Do not change those semantics without a caller contract.'),
 ('Recall rehearsal composes engines but does not qualify a product route','The example imports visits, saves traces, builds lexical/vector projections and fuses URL rankings.', ['crates/intel/eidetic-search/examples/eidetic-recall.rs','crates/intel/eidetic-search/Cargo.toml'], 'It openly labels itself a rehearsal. Import timestamps multiply arbitrary positive i64 seconds by1000 without checked overflow. Vector persistence selects the newest index globally rather than a named model/corpus identity, and embed-index zips outputs without a cardinality check before reporting all pages. Trace ESP provider/persistence contracts before promoting those larger claims.'),
 ('Search diagnostics compile production owner rather than a copied algorithm','Fresh entire library is linked into five public-API observations over exact retained suppliers.', ['crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/lib.rs','crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/bm25.rs','crates/intel/eidetic-search/src/fusion.rs'], 'Four original BM25 and five fusion source tests run alongside five integration observations,14 total. First harness build failed on an audit-only relative include; v2 compiled and ran11passing cases while3 fixture guards failed on CRLF before exercising filesystem/stem paths. V3 corrects only fixture transport and all14pass. Preserve failed receipts; no full Cargo example/ESP/live-corpus/CEF/GPU acceptance.'),
]
